<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 30,156 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 30,156 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 30,156 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday compared to 46,891 tonnes in the same period on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Sunday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   9,297	  10,411</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  20,859	  36,480</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours one was expected to sail and five were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,372	 Johar		   2/9</p>
<p>High speed diesel    73,000	 Chesa Peak City     2/9</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,045	 Oscar Acrux	   2/9</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,500	 Jin Sheng	     2/9</p>
<p>Containers		     400    Exporter		2/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
